# Avatar Omish (bouyonmusique.com, wave 25 parity, 2026-10-20)
# Sources used (all opened 2026-10-20):
# - Waitukubuli Artist Association, Omari James member page (opened): Omari Daryl James, known professionally as Avatar Omish, Dominican alternative rapper, singer and songwriter, member, listed as Singer, Rapper, Songwriter; fusion of emo rap, indie, rock and grunge; originally influenced by Christian rap; found his passion for writing songs at 14, writing amateur rap songs and recording them on his phone until he later got a laptop and mic; pivoted into different styles; performed in a NIPP Gospel competition in 2022, the Riches Karayib competition in 2023, and at numerous Lyrics Under the Star shows; released an EP called See Through Cup (no date, tracklist or platform given on the page); artist statement about making a song that could be described as undeniably beautiful. Association based in Canefield, Dominica.
# - BuzzDA, Trilla G Up Next Cypher launch article (opened, published Oct 8, 2026): Trilla-G (Gael Jno. Baptiste) through Still Trill Entertainment; Vol. 1 features Gz Up (Phillip Martin), Don Lash (Cadeem McPherson), Pa Pel (Loic Arius), Avatar Omish (Omari Dayl James), Ras B (Bayna Bellot) and Pryhmex (Ajahlie Ettienne); produced by Shane Massicott of Kwib La Beats, mixed and mastered by ThaWizZarD (Cecil Joseph Jr.); gathering on Saturday Sep 28, 2026 of young artists who had approached Trilla-G; video shot at The Lot Bar and Grill by Shane St. Claire of Sois Genial Multimedia and directed by Trilla-G and Tridel Wins Edwin; adult language note. NOTE the full name spelling here is Dayl, against Daryl on the Association page; this profile prints both spellings and flags the difference.
# - BuzzDA, One on One interview by Aliyah Jean Jacques (opened, published Oct 12, 2026): Up Next Cypher, Vol. 1 at number one on Apple Music Top Songs chart in Dominica and 83,000 YouTube views in one week; released on October 2 through Still Trill Entertainment; features Gz Up, Ras B, Avatar Omish, Don Lash, Pa Pel and Pryhmex alongside Trilla G; almost 10 minute production, instrumental by Kwib La Beats, ThaWizZarD on keys, mixing and mastering; the recorded order was kept as recorded; Gz Up breakout and his Oct 10 solo extended release; a second volume confirmed by Trilla G as planned, timing unstated.
# - YouTube, official Up Next Bouyon Cypher, Vol 1 video (search result text, 2026-10-20; direct open returned a 429 and was not retried): Still Trill Entertainment and Trilla-G present the cypher feat. Gz Up, Ras B, Avatar Omish, Don Lash, Pa Pel, Pryhmex; Apple Music and Spotify links in the description; produced by Kwib La Beats, lead keys by ThaWizZarD, mixed and mastered by ThaWizZarD; location The Lot Bar & Grill; video shot and edited by Sois Genial Multimedia.
# - Dominica Weekly, Ti Vilaj Kweyol 2026 artists (opened): 5th edition, Oct 19 to 22, 2026, Botanic Gardens, Roseau, theme Tout Biten Domnik; Oct 18 update adds a collective line spelled Gz Up, Don Lash, Avatar Omish, Papel, Prymex; no day by day schedule released as of Oct 18; Ras B is not in that collective line.
# - Waitukubuli Artist Association, Echoes of Resilience exhibition catalogue 2024 (opened): Avatar Omish and m0$h Blac, 5 minute video Bloom, playing in screening room. An art video credit, not a music release, and not carried in the structured track data.
# Note: no solo Avatar Omish artist page was verified on Spotify, Apple Music, Shazam or SoundCloud in this session, and See Through Cup has no opened platform page, so the structured track list carries only the cypher recording, verified through the official video description and the two opened BuzzDA reports.

